00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.970
I'm Rhett.
And I'm Link.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.450
This week at the Round
Table of Dim Lighting

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.550
we're going on a verbal vacation.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.900
Ah.
And to hear

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.370
you talk about it.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.920
The way I said it last time.
Teasing it last week,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.200
it sucked but you know what?

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.450
It's better to have a
good story than good time.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.718
And you know,

00:00:55.718 --> 00:00:59.010
as I've gone through all the
experiences that I have had

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.920
and then tried to figure how
I'm going to talk about them,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.960
I have realized that it was all worth it

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.420
just for this moment you know?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.530
Like whatever I went through

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.363
and however.
All right, don't put

00:01:08.363 --> 00:01:09.599
too much pressure on yourself.

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:12.450
I'm just saying that
like, I just feel like,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.890
I don't know how
entertaining it's gonna be

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.240
but I think it's gonna be very cathartic

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.060
for me just to get it all out there.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.430
Oh, but I want to give a
quick interjection, reminder.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.680
Good Mythical Evening, the second one

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.480
is happening September 1st.
Yes.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.980
Exclusively on Moment House.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.790
It's a live ticketed event,
R rated version of GMM.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.150
If you're an adult, grab yourself a ticket

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.433
at goodmythicalevening.com a'ight?

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.830
Again man, whenever
something goes sideways,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.990
it's great to have a podcast
where you know it's like,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.060
well now I know what I can talk about.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.724
I tried to keep that
in mind the whole time

00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:47.557
and I do.
You did?

00:01:47.557 --> 00:01:48.390
I do think it helps.
That's good.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.650
It's good to not be in the moment

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.020
but to be kind of like
in performance mode.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.110
And I'll just go ahead and
get started, why not right?

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:55.943
Yeah.

00:01:55.943 --> 00:02:00.090
I mean but I will say
last night, Lily asked me,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.033
I guess she was prompted by observing me.

00:02:04.685 --> 00:02:05.520
She was just watching you?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.450
Christy and I were in bed

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.283
and she comes up.
That's creepy.

00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:09.120
She comes upstairs.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.650
She's got a job.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.177
I heard about it.
She's got a summer job.

00:02:12.177 --> 00:02:13.268
She's a barista.

00:02:13.268 --> 00:02:16.290
So she comes home, she's
got her uniform on.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.460
I'm so proud of her.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.293
She comes in the room,

00:02:18.293 --> 00:02:20.370
we're asking her about
everything and then like,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.397
I was totally tucked into
bed and then she's like,

00:02:24.397 --> 00:02:26.247
"Is that how you sleep dad?"

00:02:27.506 --> 00:02:29.070
I'm glad that she's
turning out to be normal.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.450
And I'm like.
I'm just thankful for that.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.410
I'm like, "Yeah."

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.360
And I was like, "You
just use that pillow?"

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.578
I was like,

00:02:34.578 --> 00:02:35.917
"You haven't heard about
my physical therapy pillow?

00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:36.997
"Yes, this is the only,

00:02:36.997 --> 00:02:39.313
"this little log is the only thing I use."

00:02:39.313 --> 00:02:40.917
And so you like,

00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:43.067
and she's like, "So you sleep like this?"

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:46.110
And it was like a smushed
frog on a highway,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.430
like on its back.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.330
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.640
She was like, "Why are you so weird?"

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.405
Yeah, Lily's got her head on straight.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.330
And I'm like, "For your
entertainment Lily."

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.280
She was like, "Really?"

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.560
I was like, "Yeah yeah,
I live to entertain you."

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.420
I gotta hang out with Lily

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.790
for reasons that we'll
get into in a little bit.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.774
Right.

00:03:03.774 --> 00:03:05.700
Me and Jessie and Lily and her friend

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.950
actually got to go to a concert together.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.930
Yeah, I'm not happy about it.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.900
And I was.
I'm okay, I'm happy for you.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.873
Lily is, she's got her head on straight.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.320
She understands that her dad is weird.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.000
The thing that is important

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.340
is if you have a weird dad.
Yeah.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.743
You can get lost in the weirdness.

00:03:24.743 --> 00:03:26.550
Uh-huh.
And lose perspective.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.520
Or you can understand the weirdness

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.047
and just maintain some groundedness

00:03:31.047 --> 00:03:32.370
and I think that's what she's done

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.756
so I'm proud of her.
She loves me for it.

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:36.030
You know?

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.523
She's gonna keep me
around for a long time.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.950
Okay, I'll get started

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.570
'cause there's multiple steps to this.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.120
It wasn't just one trip to one place.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.120
There was multiple things that happened.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.180
So we were planning on
going to North Carolina

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.200
as the main part of this vacation.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.600
It was like go back to
North Carolina, see family.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.600
Also Jessie is working on this
vacation place slash Airbnb.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.780
We don't know exactly what it's gonna be.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.600
The vacation home that we've bought there.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.687
She's doing her design thing
on it and so we're like,

00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:15.607
"Okay, we're gonna make
the most of the time there

00:04:15.607 --> 00:04:18.600
"and stay near the cabin."

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.400
But we've got a little bit of
time in this two-week window

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.310
where we can also just do
a little family vacation.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:29.610
Let's just do something simple
like drive to Santa Barbara,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:33.736
beautiful place that's only
like 90 minutes away from us.

00:04:33.736 --> 00:04:36.720
And it would just be me and Shepherd,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.040
I mean me and Jessie and Shepherd.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.170
I don't know who put Shepherd second.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.848
Jessie and I and then our son Shepherd

00:04:43.848 --> 00:04:46.200
and Locke may or may not show up

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.120
because he's hanging out with his friend

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.937
and they're doing things and not,

00:04:49.937 --> 00:04:51.900
you know I don't know
exactly how it's gonna go.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.350
So Jessie's been very
busy, I've been very busy.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.670
So we did not do as
much of, let's just say,

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.400
vetting and research on
this particular Airbnb

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.360
that we were gonna stay at.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.670
All we knew is that it was
an incredible location,

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.230
like right on the beach.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.220
One of those situations

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.460
where you've got waves
literally at high tide

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.530
crashing into the structure

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.060
that you are sleeping in at night.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:15.893
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:15.893 --> 00:05:17.370
I mean you can't go wrong with that

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.130
unless the house falls into the ocean.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.210
But that's not my problem,

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.440
unless I'm in the house at the time.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.361
Sounds like you could be.

00:05:24.361 --> 00:05:26.021
It's a wonderful thing about renting.

00:05:26.021 --> 00:05:27.937
Of course the whole time I
was there I was thinking,

00:05:27.937 --> 00:05:29.407
"Man, what would it be
like to own this place?

00:05:29.407 --> 00:05:32.160
"I'd be constantly worried about
it falling into the ocean."

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.450
Right.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.140
So all right, there's a
couple of things that lead up

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.033
to the vacation where I,

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:44.310
we had some pictures, some old pictures

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.150
that we were getting down
from storage to go through

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:53.010
and scan some for a James
and the Shame related thing

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.180
that we're doing.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.013
Now it turns out

00:05:55.013 --> 00:05:56.994
we're not gonna use any
of these particular photos

00:05:56.994 --> 00:05:58.620
at this point.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.506
You'll understand weeks from
now what I'm talking about.

00:06:01.506 --> 00:06:04.290
So I'm carrying big things.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.970
Not just this big thing of pictures

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.470
and getting all this crap down

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.180
but I'm also like getting the suitcases

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.160
and carrying them down the stairs.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.630
I carried Jessie's suitcase.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:15.900
Whenever I do this kind of
thing, often before a vacation,

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:19.740
I end up unintentionally
stressing out my lower back.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.380
I always thought that I
was hurting my lower back

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.600
before I went on vacation
because it was a transition

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.430
and I was trying to relax
and that may be part of it

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.530
but I think it's because
I'm just carrying a lot of

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.110
right before you go on vacation.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:34.470
So when we arrive at the
place, I'm kind of like,

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.187
I'm already in a little bit
of a bad mood 'cause I'm like,

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:37.957
"Man, my back is hurting me

00:06:37.957 --> 00:06:39.817
"and I know it's gonna take 48 hours

00:06:39.817 --> 00:06:41.996
"before I can paddleboard

00:06:41.996 --> 00:06:42.829
"which is the thing I'm excited about."

00:06:42.829 --> 00:06:44.040
Is just being right there on the beach

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.920
and being able to go out there
and catch some waves man.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.090
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.370
Or at least just paddle
around like an old guy.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.870
Sure.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:56.760
But we arrive at the Airbnb and we walk in

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.913
and the first thing that we all notice,

00:07:00.761 --> 00:07:03.111
not just the tall guy is
that the ceilings are,

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.000
low.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Now I will say in the Airbnb
description it did say,

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.300
this is like the base.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.000
It's the bottom floor of a two-unit thing

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.620
and it's an old place

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.770
and the ceilings are a
little bit low in places.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.780
There's some beams or something.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.180
We didn't read it closely enough.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.080
Okay.
But what I'm saying

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.110
is that if you are over 5'9.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.590
Wow.
You would have had to duck

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:38.313
to miss these beams that are
all throughout the house.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:42.430
Also the bathroom seemed
like it was made for Hobbits

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.200
and all this was taken
with wide angle lenses

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.910
on the Airbnb listing.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:51.450
So we had really no idea it
was as extreme as it was.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.658
But then I just started walking around.

00:07:53.658 --> 00:07:54.540
They didn't have a Rhett stick

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.500
for reference?
No.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.290
Which they have here in the GMM studio.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.120
A 6'7 tall stick.
Right.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.062
That stands in for you.

00:08:02.062 --> 00:08:03.237
We need to ship the
Rhett stick ahead of time

00:08:03.237 --> 00:08:05.903
and have somebody go around
and take pictures with it.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.640
But Jessie begins taking
pictures of me and you know,

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.564
my wife is a bit of a,

00:08:16.564 --> 00:08:19.961
she knows what she's
doing on the social media.

00:08:19.961 --> 00:08:21.240
If you follow her, you know this.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.700
So she was like, "I've gotta
make this into a post."

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:26.511
She was like, "Let me just
take some pictures of you."

00:08:26.511 --> 00:08:28.237
And the only thing she
said in her tweet was,

00:08:28.237 --> 00:08:30.722
"Just arrived at our Airbnb."

00:08:30.722 --> 00:08:32.190
With three or four pictures
of me standing there

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.590
with my head completely gone because.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.747
Like behind a beam?
Behind a beam.

00:08:36.747 --> 00:08:40.800
And I don't know how many
hundreds of thousands of likes

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.270
or tweet it has at this point

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.895
but it is the most viral
tweet I've ever been

00:08:44.895 --> 00:08:46.350
in personal proximity to.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.093
I mean I've been on Twitter since,

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.701
I don't know, well over a decade.

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:52.961
We have a lot of professional tweets.

00:08:52.961 --> 00:08:55.410
And I am a relatively
internet famous person.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.300
Never had a viral tweet.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.210
My wife just farts one out.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:02.223
Of course as I told her, I was in it.

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:05.407
Of course you couldn't see my face.

00:09:05.407 --> 00:09:06.240
I mean your bottom half.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.073
She did not tag me.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.760
So anyway, while she got
a viral tweet out of it

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.010
which was pretty awesome.

00:09:14.566 --> 00:09:16.410
We immediately began to,

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.930
I had taken all this
stuff down these stairs.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.790
Like you had to come downstairs

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.640
to get to the unit where
you could go in the side

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.410
and then go around and get in there.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.643
And I'm settled in.

00:09:27.601 --> 00:09:29.430
And she's mad, she's happy about the tweet

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.350
but she's mad about the situation.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.467
And she says,

00:09:32.467 --> 00:09:34.177
"I just think we should,

00:09:34.177 --> 00:09:35.988
"we should just go somewhere else.

00:09:35.988 --> 00:09:38.347
"You're not gonna be
able to enjoy yourself,

00:09:38.347 --> 00:09:41.294
"you're gonna be ducking
around this thing."

00:09:41.294 --> 00:09:44.460
Oh it's only one bathroom.

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.020
This is something that was in the listing

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:51.020
that we just didn't really
look at and it's technically,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.480
it's got four bunk beds that are outside

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.630
in the living room area kind of?

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.240
So Shepherd was gonna be
sleeping in this bunk bed

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.260
that's kind of out in the open

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.637
and then sharing a bathroom with us.

00:10:02.637 --> 00:10:06.015
And 13-year-old needs privacy
if you know what I mean?

00:10:06.015 --> 00:10:07.051
Okay.
You know what I'm saying?

00:10:07.051 --> 00:10:09.510
And so you could kind of tell

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:12.317
that he's a little bit antsy
and then Jessie's like,

00:10:12.317 --> 00:10:14.107
"We'll just try to find a hotel.

00:10:14.107 --> 00:10:15.911
"We can get our money back for the."

00:10:15.911 --> 00:10:17.707
And I'm like, "We've already
moved all our stuff in.

00:10:17.707 --> 00:10:19.237
"I'm the tall one.

00:10:19.237 --> 00:10:22.069
"I'm the one who should be
complaining and I'm not.

00:10:22.069 --> 00:10:24.267
"Let's just try to enjoy ourselves."

00:10:25.545 --> 00:10:27.483
Not a great way to start a vacation.

00:10:27.483 --> 00:10:28.530
Yeah.
Yelling at each other

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:31.650
about how you need to
try to enjoy yourself.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.810
And she couldn't think of other ways

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.480
to continue to make more viral tweets.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.012
It's kind of like.

00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:40.717
You go into that, you
dig that well one time.

00:10:40.717 --> 00:10:42.028
You know what I'm saying?
Yep.

00:10:42.028 --> 00:10:43.187
So, but I was like,

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:45.930
there's a lot to love about this.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.750
